From db0f5a3d530204e2f053f9d7ada6e385c312f8ff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?St=C3=A9phane=20Payrard?= <cognominal@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:30:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat: hover help explains the rail and the panes

Hover help now explains the rail, one part per section the last frame
drew, and every pane on the workspace, with its title bar and its body
as parts. A section's keys are the ones that act while the rail has the
keyboard. A hidden rail keeps a page with no rectangle, so the walk
still reaches the key that shows it.

The walk tests reach the desktop with shift+left now, since the rail
and the panes sit between the dock and the desktop.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 e2e/tui/hover_help_test.go       |  98 +++++++++-
 internal/app/hover_help.go       |   2 +
 internal/app/hover_help_parts.go | 301 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 391 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 internal/app/hover_help_parts.go

